# AMD64 thunk export spec for the guest mfmediaengine.dll -- COM mode.
#
# COM-JSON is ppc64le/mf/interfaces_mf.json, the SAME file dlls/mfplat,
# dlls/mf and dlls/mfreadwrite name.  Every guest module on this surface
# publishes an identical roster, which is what lets the one winecom instance
# in native mfplat.dll serve a proxy whose vtable came from any of them --
# and it is why IMFMediaEngine joined that roster rather than getting one of
# its own.  A media engine is handed IMFAttributes and IMFMediaType objects
# that mfplat minted; a second roster would make those a different surface's
# proxies and the first SetSource would be refused as a guest-implemented
# object.  mfmediaengine.spec forwards __wine_com_dispatch into mfplat for
# the same reason mf.spec and mfreadwrite.spec do: there can be only one
# instance.
#
# WHAT THIS MODULE IS FOR.  IMFMediaEngine is the HTML5-shaped player -- load
# a URL, play, seek, ask for the current frame -- and it is what a game's
# video plugin reaches for when it wants a cutscene without building a
# topology by hand.  ppc64le/mf/README.md used to record it as "not a blocker
# in principle, since reverse proxies exist; it is a separate roster and a
# separate module, and nothing in the corpus has asked for it yet."  It is now
# the same roster and no longer a separate module.
#
# THE CALLBACK IS THE POINT, and it is the reverse direction.  The engine is
# useless without IMFMediaEngineNotify: the application implements it and
# Media Foundation calls EventNotify from its own thread for every state
# change.  That is a guest-implemented object handed into native code, which
# is precisely what libs/winecom/reverse.c builds a native vtable for, and
# what dlls/mfplat/mfcom.c turns on with WINECOM_SF_REVERSE.  The notify
# object arrives through IMFMediaEngineClassFactory::CreateInstance's
# attribute store (MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_CALLBACK), by the same road
# MF_SOURCE_READER_ASYNC_CALLBACK already travels.
#
# THE FLAT SURFACE IS THREE ENTRIES and only one of them carries an
# interface.  DllCanUnloadNow takes nothing; DllGetActivationFactory is a stub
# in the .spec and spec2thunk emits nothing for a stub; DllGetClassObject is
# the door, and it gets the same riid/void** wrapper every other module's has.
DLL mfmediaengine.dll
FROM-SPEC auto

PROBE-EXTRA mfapi.h
PROBE-EXTRA mfidl.h
PROBE-EXTRA mfmediaengine.h
PROBE-EXTRA mferror.h

COM-JSON  ../../ppc64le/mf/interfaces_mf.json

GUEST-IMPL   DllGetClassObject                     __wine_guest_DllGetClassObject
